WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.285
Hi, I'm Sorbet!

00:00:02.285 --> 00:00:05.603
Prime Agent gives its model one tool, a Python kernel.

00:00:05.603 --> 00:00:07.262
Here's what sits behind it.

00:00:09.808 --> 00:00:12.942
The idea: one tool, a persistent Python kernel.

00:00:12.942 --> 00:00:15.292
Loops, files and subagents become code.

00:00:15.292 --> 00:00:18.817
The schema doesn't vanish; it moves behind the kernel.

00:00:20.525 --> 00:00:24.128
A usual harness re-sends every tool schema with each request, and each

00:00:24.128 --> 00:00:26.531
step of a loop costs a model turn.

00:00:26.951 --> 00:00:30.274
Here, a loop over sixty files is one call, and its results

00:00:30.274 --> 00:00:31.936
stay in a variable for later.

00:00:34.008 --> 00:00:36.595
The model writes a string of code.

00:00:36.595 --> 00:00:40.660
A persistent IPython kernel runs it, and variables, imports and open

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:42.139
files survive between turns.

00:00:42.559 --> 00:00:47.008
Files, shell and MCP servers are plain Python, run with your permissions.

00:00:47.008 --> 00:00:48.861
That half really is unbounded.

00:00:49.281 --> 00:00:50.745
Agent control is different.

00:00:50.745 --> 00:00:55.138
Spawning a child or opening a goal crosses to the TypeScript host:

00:00:55.138 --> 00:00:58.067
twenty-one typed handlers, most on only by flag.

00:00:58.487 --> 00:01:02.133
A spawned child returns a handle at once, works in its own

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:03.955
session, and reports back by message.

00:01:05.858 --> 00:01:08.982
State that outlives a turn goes through one command: refine.

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:11.943
It reads the trajectory and past refinements.

00:01:12.363 --> 00:01:16.707
It proposes small edits: prompt notes, memories, skills, subagent roles.

00:01:17.127 --> 00:01:20.869
Host code, not a prompt, rejects any edit to the base system prompt.

00:01:21.289 --> 00:01:25.198
Every pass is logged, so a bad edit rolls back to a recorded version.

00:01:26.475 --> 00:01:28.601
Prime Agent didn't abolish the tool schema.

00:01:28.601 --> 00:01:32.548
It demoted it, out of the prompt and into a private typed bridge.

00:01:35.192 --> 00:01:38.531
To recap: one kernel, a typed bridge, and a harness that

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:39.745
can't rewrite its rules.

00:01:40.165 --> 00:01:42.310
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:42.922
I'm Sorbet.

00:01:42.922 --> 00:01:43.229
Bye!
